# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_column_substrate.py" "COLUMN-SUBSTRATE GATE: PASS" "column-substrate: additive column-level DDL and explicit-SQL extraction in _cg_schema (column nodes + alters_col/queries_col edges); table-level coupling regression-clean; recall-safe on SELECT-star and ORM-only files" "column-substrate precision (fix/column-level-substrate, 2026-06-20): the action_required pause tier uses table-level shared-resource coupling to BLOCK a PR until acknowledged. Table-level coupling is too coarse when two PRs edit DIFFERENT columns of the SAME large table (false pause). This gate covers the additive column-level substrate: WHERE COLUMNS ARE CLEANLY KNOWN from raw DDL, column nodes (kind=column, id=column::T.C) and column-granular edges (alters_col from DDL files, queries_col from code files with explicit SELECT col/UPDATE SET col SQL) are minted IN ADDITION TO the existing table-level nodes and edges. Table-level nodes and edges are BYTE-FOR-BYTE UNCHANGED -- the live pause tier MUST NOT regress. RECALL-SAFE: SELECT-star and ORM-only files (no explicit SQL columns) produce NO column edges, only the table-level edge is kept (coupling not lost). Precision-first for the column layer: only unambiguous DDL (CREATE TABLE col list, ALTER ADD COLUMN) and explicit SQL forms (SELECT col-list FROM t, UPDATE t SET col=) emit column edges -- bare attribute access / SELECT-star / column-less ORM calls do NOT emit column edges (the measured 60-80% false-coupling rate for bare column names is why; gate 92 column_impact boundary respected). Edge kinds: alters_col and queries_col (distinct from the table-level alters/queries so the existing gate-92 and test_extractor flood-bound assertions remain unaffected). No DB, no network. Content-free: column NAMES only. Hermetic synthetic fixtures + never-crash pathological inputs (empty, binary-ish, deeply-nested parens, oversized col list bounded by _MAX_COLUMNS=500)." "column-substrate: column nodes + alters_col/queries_col edges additive on raw DDL and explicit SQL; table-level edges byte-for-byte unchanged; SELECT-star and ORM-only files recall-safe (table coupling kept, no spurious column edges); bounded and never-crash" 12
